    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "James Whitney became the first permanent settler in Ludlow in 1784, establishing a homestead near the Black River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Ludlow_(town),_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The arrival of the Rutland and Burlington Railroad in 1849 connected Ludlow to broader markets and boosted exports of manufactured goods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Ludlow_(town),_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ludlow originally operated as a mill town focused on woolen production before transitioning to a tourism-based economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Ludlow_(town),_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Okemo Mountain Resort opened in Ludlow on January 31, 1956, following an eleven-inch snowstorm.",
